ENTRY 11117 {"id":11117,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"     1\t/* global process, fetch, console, AbortController, setTimeout, clearTimeout, TextDecoder */\n     2\t// Tiny session-API client for tests/e2e/run-phase4b.sh. Runs inside an ingest pod (`kubectl exec -i ... node - ...`), where\n     3\t// PI_API_TOKENS is already in the environment, so no token ever leaves the cluster or is printed. For a local stack\n     4\t// set API_BASE and PI_API_TOKENS (or API_TOKEN) in the environment.\n     5\t//\n     6\t//   node client.mjs call OWNER METHOD PATH [BODY]  -> {\"status\":N,\"body\":...}\n     7\t//   node client.mjs stream OWNER SESSION NEEDLE SECONDS -> prints \"found\" or \"timeout\"; exit 0 either way\n     8\t//   node client.mjs dump OWNER SESSION SECONDS -> the raw event stream, for debugging\n     9\t//   node client.mjs answer OWNER SESSION NEEDLE SECONDS -> prints \"found <tools>\" when an ASSISTANT text contains\n    10\t//     NEEDLE after at least one tool call (<tools> = number of calls seen), else \"timeout\" or \"failed\"\n    11\tconst base = process.env.API_BASE ?? \"http://127.0.0.1:8080\";\n    12\t\n    13\tfunction tokenFor(owner) {\n    14\t  if (process.env.API_TOKEN) return process.env.API_TOKEN;\n    15\t  for (const line of (process.env.PI_API_TOKENS ?? \"\").split(\"\\n\")) {\n    16\t    const [name, token] = line.trim().split(\":\");\n    17\t    if (name === owner && token) return token;\n    18\t  }\n    19\t  throw new Error(`no token for owner ${owner}`);\n    20\t}\n    21\t\n    22\tconst [command, owner, ...rest] = process.argv.slice(2);\n    23\tconst headers = { authorization: `Bearer ${tokenFor(owner)}`, \"content-type\": \"application/json\" };\n    24\t\n    25\tif (command === \"call\") {\n    26\t  const [method, path, body] = rest;\n    27\t  const response = await fetch(base + path, { method, headers, body: body || undefined });\n    28\t  const text = await response.text();\n    29\t  let parsed = null;\n    30\t  try {\n    31\t    parsed = JSON.parse(text);\n    32\t  } catch {\n    33\t    // Not JSON (an empty body): report the status only.\n    34\t  }\n    35\t  console.log(JSON.stringify({ status: response.status, body: parsed }));\n    36\t} else if (command === \"stream\") {\n    37\t  const [session, needle, seconds] = rest;\n    38\t  const controller = new AbortController();\n    39\t  const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), Number(seconds) * 1000);\n    40\t  let seen = \"\";\n    41\t  let found = false;\n    42\t  try {\n    43\t    const response = await fetch(`${base}/sessions/${session}/stream`, {\n    44\t      headers: { ...headers, accept: \"text/event-stream\" },\n    45\t      signal: controller.signal,\n    46\t    });\n    47\t    const decoder = new TextDecoder();\n    48\t    for await (const chunk of response.body) {\n    49\t      seen += decoder.decode(chunk, { stream: true });\n    50\t      if (seen.toLowerCase().includes(needle.toLowerCase())) {\n    51\t        found = true;\n    52\t        break;\n    53\t      }\n    54\t    }\n    55\t  } catch {\n    56\t    // Aborted by the timer.\n    57\t  }\n    58\t  clearTimeout(timer);\n    59\t  controller.abort();\n    60\t  console.log(found ? \"found\" : \"timeout\");\n    61\t} else if (command === \"dump\") {\n    62\t  // Debugging aid: print the raw event stream for SECONDS (entries and live state; no secrets pass through here).\n    63\t  const [session, seconds] = rest;\n    64\t  const controller = new AbortController();\n    65\t  setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), Number(seconds) * 1000);\n    66\t  try {\n    67\t    const response = await fetch(`${base}/sessions/${session}/stream`, {\n    68\t      headers: { ...headers, accept: \"text/event-stream\" },\n    69\t      signal: controller.signal,\n    70\t    });\n    71\t    const decoder = new TextDecoder();\n    72\t    for await (const chunk of response.body)\n    73\t      process.stdout.write(decoder.decode(chunk, { stream: true }));\n    74\t  } catch {\n    75\t    // Aborted by the timer.\n    76\t  }\n    77\t} else if (command === \"answer\") {\n    78\t  const [session, needle, seconds] = rest;\n    79\t  const controller = new AbortController();\n    80\t  const timer = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), Number(seconds) * 1000);\n    81\t  let buffer = \"\";\n    82\t  let calls = 0;\n    83\t  let result = \"timeout\";\n    84\t  try {\n    85\t    const response = await fetch(`${base}/sessions/${session}/stream`, {\n    86\t      headers: { ...headers, accept: \"text/event-stream\" },\n    87\t      signal: controller.signal,\n    88\t    });\n    89\t    const decoder = new TextDecoder();\n    90\t    outer: for await (const chunk of response.body) {\n    91\t      buffer += decoder.decode(chunk, { stream: true });\n    92\t      let end;\n    93\t      while ((end = buffer.indexOf(\"\\n\\n\")) >= 0) {\n    94\t        const block = buffer.slice(0, end);\n    95\t        buffer = buffer.slice(end + 2);\n    96\t        if (!block.includes(\"event: entry\")) continue;\n    97\t        const data = block.split(\"\\n\").find((line) => line.startsWith(\"data: \"));\n    98\t        const entry = JSON.parse(data.slice(6));\n    99\t        for (const message of entry.messages ?? []) {\n   100\t          if (message.role !== \"assistant\") continue;\n   101\t          calls += (message.calls ?? []).length;\n   102\t          if (calls > 0 && (message.text ?? \"\").toLowerCase().includes(needle.toLowerCase())) {\n   103\t            result = `found ${calls}`;\n   104\t            break outer;\n   105\t          }\n   106\t        }\n   107\t      }\n   108\t    }\n   109\t  } catch {\n   110\t    // Aborted by the timer.\n   111\t  }\n   112\t  clearTimeout(timer);\n   113\t  controller.abort();\n   114\t  console.log(result);\n   115\t} else {\n   116\t  throw new Error(\"usage: call|stream|dump|answer\");\n   117\t}\n/bin/bash: line 1: rg: command not found\n<harness>\n[error] Command exited with code 127\n</harness>","isError":true}]}
ENTRY 11151 {"id":11151,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]","calls":["bash({\"command\":\"bash -c 'set -euo pipefail; f=$(mktemp); trap '\\\\''x=$(grep -v \\\"^$\\\" \\\"$f\\\" | sed \\\"s/.*/x/\\\" | paste -sd, -); echo cleaned; rm \\\"$f\\\"'\\\\'' EXIT; echo success'; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"; cd /workspace/repo && sed -n '87,119p;197,220p;224,266p' tests/e2e/run-phase4b.sh && grep -n 'phase4b\\\\|run-phase4b' tests/e2e/run.sh\",\"timeout\":10000})"]}]}
ENTRY 11155 {"id":11155,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"success\nexit=1\ncleanup() {\n  local id\n  while read -r id; do\n    [[ -n $id ]] || continue\n    api alice DELETE \"/sessions/$id\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true\n  done <\"$sessions_file\"\n  # The delete is asynchronous (the orchestrator removes the sandbox first): wait (bounded) until every session is\n  # `deleted`, then drop the rows of the sessions that got there. Dropping a row earlier would orphan a claim the\n  # delete had not reached yet, so the others are reported and kept. A failed query is not \"nothing left\": it is\n  # retried until the deadline.\n  local list deadline pending status\n  list=$(grep -v '^$' \"$sessions_file\" | sed \"s/.*/'&'/\" | paste -sd, -)\n  deadline=$(($(now) + 180))\n  while [[ -n $list && $(now) -lt $deadline ]]; do\n    if pending=$(sql \"select id from inbox.sessions where status <> 'deleted' and id in ($list)\" 2>/dev/null) && [[ -z $pending ]]; then\n      break\n    fi\n    sleep 3\n  done\n  while read -r id; do\n    [[ -n $id ]] || continue\n    if ! status=$(sql \"select status from inbox.sessions where id='$id'\" 2>/dev/null | tr -d ' '; exit \"${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"); then\n      note \"cleanup: could not read the status of session $id; keeping its rows\"\n    elif [[ -z $status || $status == deleted ]]; then\n      sql \"delete from inbox.events where session_id='$id'; delete from inbox.sessions where id='$id'\" >/dev/null 2>&1 ||\n        note \"cleanup: could not delete the rows of session $id\"\n    else\n      note \"cleanup: session $id is still '$status' after the wait; keeping its rows (its claim may remain)\"\n    fi\n  done <\"$sessions_file\"\n  rm -rf \"$work\"\n}\ntrap cleanup EXIT\nt_failed_401() {\n  local c id restarts out text\n  c=$(new_session alice)\n  id=$(jq -r .body.sessionId <<<\"$c\")\n  restarts=$(orch_restarts)\n  text=$(jq -cn '{kind:\"message\", text:({steps:[], error:\"401 Unauthorized: simulated rejected credentials\"}|tostring)}')\n  api alice POST \"/sessions/$id/events\" \"$text\" >/dev/null\n  out=$(wait_status alice \"$id\" failed 90) || exit 1\n  assert_jq \"the session is failed, with a clear message\" \"$out\" '.body.status==\"failed\" and (.body.failure|test(\"401/403\")) and (.body.failure|test(\"OneCLI\"))'\n  assert_jq \"the failure message does not repeat the provider's text\" \"$out\" '(.body.failure|test(\"simulated\")|not)'\n  out=$(api alice POST \"/sessions/$id/events\" '{\"kind\":\"message\",\"text\":\"again\"}')\n  assert_jq \"further input is refused with 409\" \"$out\" '.status==409'\n  sleep 15\n  assert_eq \"the orchestrator did not restart\" \"$restarts\" \"$(orch_restarts)\"\n  assert_eq \"the event was submitted once, not retried\" \"1|submitted\" \"$(sql \"select attempts||'|'||status from inbox.events where session_id='$id' and kind='message' and payload->>'text' like '%401%'\")\"\n  assert_eq \"the session stays failed\" failed \"$(sql \"select status from inbox.sessions where id='$id'\")\"\n  if orch_log | grep -q -E 'fail-closed|\"event\":\"fatal\"'; then\n    note \"ASSERT FAILED: the orchestrator logged a fatal or fail-closed event\"\n    exit 1\n  fi\n  note \"ok: no fatal or fail-closed event in the orchestrator log\"\n  out=$(api alice DELETE \"/sessions/$id\")\n  assert_jq \"a failed session can still be deleted\" \"$out\" '.status==202'\n  wait_status alice \"$id\" deleted 60 >/dev/null || exit 1\nt_real_model() {\n  # OpenAI Codex (ChatGPT subscription) through OneCLI. The default pair is in the committed ConfigMap's allowlist.\n  local models=${REAL_MODELS:-openai-codex/gpt-6.1-terra,openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol}\n  local entry provider model out id answer\n  if [[ $mode == local ]]; then\n    note \"SKIPPED: the real-model test needs the cluster (MODE=cluster)\"\n    return 3\n  fi\n  if ! k get secret pi-onecli >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    note \"SKIPPED: Secret pi-onecli does not exist in the namespace (ExternalSecret pi-onecli, key agent-token).\"\n    note \"  See docs/model-credentials.md, Set up.\"\n    return 3\n  fi\n  note \"ok: pi-onecli delivered by the ExternalSecret\"\n  # Names only, never values: no provider credential is in the orchestrator's environment.\n  if k exec deploy/pi-orchestrator -- sh -c 'env | cut -d= -f1' | grep -q -E '^(OPENROUTER|OPENAI|ANTHROPIC)_API_KEY$'; then\n    note \"ASSERT FAILED: a provider API key is in the orchestrator environment\"\n    exit 1\n  fi\n  note \"ok: no provider API key in the orchestrator environment\"\n  for entry in ${models//,/ }; do\n    provider=${entry%%/*}\n    model=${entry#*/}\n    out=$(new_session alice \"$(jq -cn --arg p \"$provider\" --arg m \"$model\" '{provider:$p, model:$m}')\")\n    assert_jq \"session created on $entry\" \"$out\" '.status==201'\n    id=$(jq -r .body.sessionId <<<\"$out\")\n    # printf splits the word, so the user's own message does not contain the needle.\n    api alice POST \"/sessions/$id/events\" \\\n      '{\"kind\":\"message\",\"text\":\"Run `printf \\\"hel%s\\\" lo` in the sandbox and tell me exactly what it printed.\"}' >/dev/null\n    answer=$(answer_has alice \"$id\" hello 180)\n    case $answer in\n      found*) note \"ok: $entry answered with the tool output after ${answer#found } tool call(s)\" ;;\n      *)\n        note \"ASSERT FAILED: $entry did not answer with the tool output ($answer)\"\n        exit 1\n        ;;\n    esac\n    assert_jq \"the session is still active\" \"$(api alice GET \"/sessions/$id\")\" '.body.status==\"active\"'\n    if orch_log | grep -q -E 'aoc_|eyJ|sk-'; then\n      note \"ASSERT FAILED: the orchestrator log holds something shaped like a token or key\"\n      exit 1\n    fi\n    note \"ok: no aoc_, JWT or sk- shaped text in the orchestrator log\"\n2:# Single entry point for the e2e suites: tests/e2e/run.sh <smoke|phase1|phase3|phase4|phase4b|phase4c|all>\n4:#   phase4b per-session models, allowlist, terminal failure on rejected credentials; REAL_MODEL=1 adds two real\n8:#   all     the full failure suite: phase1, phase3, phase4 and phase4b (the real-model test only with REAL_MODEL=1)\n45:phase4b) phases=(phase4b) ;;\n47:all) phases=(phase1 phase3 phase4 phase4b) ;;\n49:  echo \"usage: tests/e2e/run.sh <smoke|phase1|phase3|phase4|phase4b|phase4c|all>\" >&2\n88:if has_phase phase3 || has_phase phase4 || has_phase phase4b || has_phase phase4c; then\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 11230 {"id":11230,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"## Findings\n\n### 1. Cleanup fails when no sessions were created\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: tests/e2e/run-phase4b.sh:98\n- What happens: A successful run with `ONLY=disallowed`, or a run where the real-model test is skipped and no other test runs, reaches cleanup with an empty sessions file. `grep` returns 1, so `set -e` aborts the EXIT trap, changes the script’s exit status to failure, and leaves the temporary directory behind.\n- Evidence: `list=$(grep -v '^$' \"$sessions_file\" | sed \"s/.*/'&'/\" | paste -sd, -)`\n- Fix idea: Treat an empty sessions file as a normal case when building `list`, and ensure cleanup still removes the temporary directory.\n\n### 2. Failed inspection commands can pass security and log assertions\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: tests/e2e/run-phase4b.sh:239\n- What happens: If `kubectl exec` fails, the environment check reports that no provider key is present even though it could not inspect the environment. The log checks at lines 213 and 262 similarly report success when fetching orchestrator logs fails. With `pipefail`, an upstream command terminated after `grep -q` finds a match can also make a matching pipeline appear unsuccessful.\n- Evidence: `if k exec deploy/pi-orchestrator -- sh -c 'env | cut -d= -f1' | grep -q -E ...; then`\n- Fix idea: Capture and validate the inspection command’s output and exit status separately, then search the captured output. Fail the test if inspection fails.\n\n### 3. Secret lookup errors are reported as a legitimate skip\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: tests/e2e/run-phase4b.sh:232\n- What happens: When the real-model test is requested, a Kubernetes authorization error, API outage, or other `kubectl` failure is reported as the secret being absent. The test is skipped rather than failed, potentially yielding a successful acceptance run without exercising real models.\n- Evidence: `if ! k get secret pi-onecli >/dev/null 2>&1; then`\n- Fix idea: Distinguish a genuine NotFound response from other lookup failures, and fail the test for errors that prevent determining whether the secret exists.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
DONE
